Prompt: critic_continuity.j2
Service Step: CRITIC_CONTINUITY (Continuity Critique)
Function Overview: Cross-chapter continuity reviewer, checking for continuity issues between "previous chapter → current chapter".
Upstream Inputs:
  - chapter_number: Chapter number
  - previous_chapter: Previous chapter body (last paragraph context)
  - previous_chapter_ending: Previous chapter ending (original text)
  - current_chapter: Current chapter body
  - canon_state_summary: Canon summary (read-only reference)
Downstream Outputs:
  - JSON: {"issues": [{"severity", "summary", "evidence", "suggested_fix", "confidence"}]}
  - Downstream Consumer: Memory System / ContinuityRepairStep
Consumption Chain Priority: P0 (Opening Handoff Break / Amnesiac State Jump) > P1 (Emotion/Action Handoff Break)
              > P2 (Planning Terminology Intrusion)
Brief Example:
  Input: chapter_number=5, previous_chapter_ending="Lin Yuan gripped the sword hilt"
  Output: {"issues": [{"severity": "high", "summary": "This chapter's opening location doesn't match previous chapter's ending", "evidence": "...", "confidence": 0.85}]}
